   "notes": {
    "ammo": "Measured on four weapon shapes, all within a few points of this table: the first volleys land while it matters most. The interior keeps attack × N ÷ {ammoRounds} until it is measured",
    "armor": "**Armor** at Mk I is {armor} health with no effect. It has **Vulnerable (Plasma)**, worth about {vulnOther} BP because Plasma is rarer than Kinetic (assuming about 15% of weapons are Plasma).",
    "attackExt": "Measured: 2/8 worth 14, 4/8 worth 24, 6/8 worth 31",
    "attackInt": "A chosen scale, not a measured one: crew only fight boarders, and those fights are thresholds (the defender acts first, so equal crews stall), so a point of crew attack or health is worth almost nothing at the margin. At this scale a plain Mk I crew card is about 4/12",
    "bigHit": "More of a big hit is wasted to overkill: worth per point measured 3.9 at 6 per hit, 3.3 at 12, 3.1 at 16",
    "block": "Stops an attack outright; about 3 health each, in front or behind",
    "buffIntro": "Measured in the simulator (Mk I, exterior rows, 2026-09-30): what a buff is worth in health BP, next to 24 BP weapons of every shape. The card editor prices these effects on its own, by the card's placement; everything else goes in Effect BP.",
    "buffOther": "Other buffs measured the same way: +1 attack to all your weapons about 30 (5 a weapon). A full interior of six +1 mult cards shortens mirrored fights from about 13 rounds to 7.",
    "extraHitExt": "An extra hit is worth more the harder it hits: 1×3 measured 16 in attack, 3×2 measured 31. It evens out ×1, ×2 and ×3 shapes (51, 49, 47% in random mixes)",
    "extraHitInt": "Kept from the older rule: crew fights are thresholds (Attack and health, interior)",
    "frontHealth": "A card that must sit in front of the armor, or an exterior Defense card with no attack. Health there is hit first and buys the most time: a 24-health wall is worth about 41. Replaces the old +6 budget for front-only weapons",
    "health": "Behind the armor. Measured: 1 a point on average, more right behind the armor, almost nothing at the back",
    "hull": "Measured: +2 and +3 hull worth about 1, +10 about 2. In exterior fights hull only buys time, and against boarders more hull barely helps either",
    "intBuffIntro": "**Interior buffs on the weapon above** (measured 2026-09-30 against reference weapons, Mk I, on a 24 BP weapon right behind the Armor and at the back). An interior card's only adjacent weapon is the one above it, so \"adjacent\" effects on an interior card are priced as one weapon. They are worth about what the same buff is worth beside an exterior weapon, so the two tables agree.",
    "m.activate": "19–34 behind the armor (about 1.5 × the target's attack BP); 4–10 in front, where its target is exposed too",
    "m.attackAdjacent": "8–10 next to single-hit weapons, 21–33 next to multi-hit ones",
    "m.attackAdjacentMult": "21–33",
    "m.attackOne": "4 per point per hit; about 5 on multi-hit targets, which waste less damage",
    "m.doubleOnBehind": "17–24: the card shields its target but dies sooner, and the buff ends with it",
    "m.doubleOnFront": "23–34: the card sits safe behind its target",
    "maxHealth": "Same as health",
    "mi.activate": "13–22",
    "mi.aim": "13–18",
    "mi.ammoMax": "0–4",
    "mi.attack": "2–5 on single hits, 10–20 on a 1×3",
    "mi.double": "11–17",
    "mi.healthRepair": "+3 health 2–4; repair 2 a round 1–3",
    "mi.hull": "+2 or +3: 1; +10: 2",
    "mi.mult": "+1: 16–23 (13 in front of the Armor, 10 on a 2×2, 4–9 on a 1×3); +2: 30–44",
    "mi.resistPierce": "Resist 1: 2–6; Pierce: about 0",
    "mi.shieldsRound": "+2 a round: 5",
    "pierce": "Measured about 0: it hits the card under its target, and for the first rounds that is under the Shields, the front card and the Armor. By the time it reaches a support card under a weapon, the weapon is dying anyway. Pierce needs a new job before it is worth more",
    "plasmaInt": "Kept from the older rule: crew fights are thresholds (Attack and health, interior)",
    "reflect": "Reflect 1 on the Armor was worth about 4.5 health; Reflect 2 about 13, because it kills small multi-hit weapons",
    "regen": "Repairs or heals N each time it activates while alive; never brings a destroyed card back. Read from the effect text",
    "resist": "Every instance of damage is N lower. Measured: 10–16 a point on a front wall, 7–10 on a front weapon, about 8 on the Armor, 4–6 behind the armor. Resist 2 is worth more than twice Resist 1, and more against multi-hit, low-attack enemies",
    "restore": "After a round with no damage, restores N each time it activates, even from 0 on a card that goes down rather than being destroyed. Every Shields card has Restore 1 per mark",
    "shields": "Restore 1 is worth about {restore} BP: at equal points, a restoring Shields card beats a non-restoring one 70% of the time, restoring 3 to 4 times a fight, and each restored point swallows a whole attack. **Vulnerable (Kinetic)** costs about {vulnK}. Net, a plain Shields card is {shields} shield points.",
    "splash": "Not measured yet",
    "thermalInt": "Fire burns inside only; radiation reaches Biological crew",
    "typeExt": "Against Kinetic, whose +1 against Shields is already in the attack rate. Plasma's bonus against armor and hull only matches it; Radiation needs Biological targets; each Electric hit on a surviving Shields card gives it a shield point back",
    "vuln": "A printed weakness; read from the card text"
   }
